{%- comment -%}
  fye-gem-icon — a gemstone as a drawn brilliant cut.

  Added 05/09/2026. Replaces the flat colour field (fye-swatch-block, kind:
  'gem') on the matchmaker's stone step.

  WHY. Sixteen coloured rectangles side by side read as a paint chart. Every
  other step in the matchmaker shows a photograph of a real ring; the stone step
  cannot, because a photograph of a sapphire ring shows the setting as much as
  the stone. So the stone gets drawn instead: one round brilliant, viewed from
  above, rendered sixteen times in sixteen colourways. Same cut every time,
  deliberately — the question asks which MATERIAL, not which cut, and varying
  the cut would imply a ruby comes marquise and an emerald comes emerald-cut.

  Facets do the work colour cannot. Table, star and bezel facets differ in tone
  the way a real stone's do, which is what makes a diamond legible at all
  (colourless, so its structure is the only thing to see) and a black diamond
  legible too.

  USAGE
    {%- render 'fye-gem-icon', name: 'Sapphire', class: 'rfd__oicon' -%}

  The artwork lives in assets/ as one SVG per stone, not inlined here: sixteen
  inlined stones would add ~43KB to every render of this page, and as separate
  assets they are cached once and reused by the filter rail later.

  NAME MAPPING. The finder's option labels carry qualifiers the stone itself
  does not — "Blue Topaz" IS topaz, "Pink Tourmaline" IS tourmaline — so both
  map to one file. An unrecognised name renders NOTHING rather than a broken
  image: the tile then shows its label alone, which is a degraded tile rather
  than a broken one.

  Kept out of a case block on purpose. The first version of the swatch snippet
  put comments inside a Liquid case and threw "Case tag must be followed by
  exactly one 'when'", blanking the whole section. A handle filter does the
  same job with nothing to get wrong.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign key = name | strip | downcase | replace: ' ', '-'
  if key == 'blue-topaz'
    assign key = 'topaz'
  endif
  if key == 'pink-tourmaline'
    assign key = 'tourmaline'
  endif

  assign known = 'diamond,ruby,sapphire,emerald,tanzanite,aquamarine,morganite,peridot,amethyst,garnet,citrine,topaz,tourmaline,opal,fire-opal,black-diamond' | split: ','
  assign ok = false
  for k in known
    if k == key
      assign ok = true
      break
    endif
  endfor

  assign file = 'fye-gem-' | append: key | append: '.svg'
-%}
{%- if ok -%}
  <img class="fic fic--gem fic--gem-{{ key }} {{ class }}"
       src="{{ file | asset_url }}"
       alt=""
       width="200" height="200"
       loading="lazy" decoding="async">
{%- endif -%}
